{"parentUuid":"42b80ca1-14f8-47ad-b284-19b2326daefb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8b962ec7-f6f2-48a1-9f71-621868530ef7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"  Task Overview\n\n  Review whether the current redaction patch is worth keeping,\n  especially the extra tests/policy around account/id values.\n  Original concern was leaked transcript/log content around:\n\n  - GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET\n  - shell transcript shape like printf 'secret...' | npx wrangler\n    secret put WIRO_API_KEY\n  - possible npx wrangler containers ssh <opaque token> confusion\n  - Application ID\n  - GOOGLE_ADSENSE_ACCOUNT\n\n  Main user concern: avoid over-redaction and avoid cluttering the\n  redaction tests with incident-specific cases.\n\n  Current State\n\n  Worktree: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/\n  cli/.worktrees/redact-2\n\n  Files changed:\n\n  - redact/redact.go\n  - redact/redact_test.go\n\n  Current patch adds generalized secret-key redaction for names\n  like API_KEY, TOKEN, CLIENT_SECRET, SSH_KEY, etc. It also adds\n  shell-stdin detection for:\n\n  printf 'REDACTED' | examplectl secret put EXAMPLE_API_KEY\n\n  This is intentionally not Wrangler-specific and not WIRO-\n  specific.\n\n  Important Discoveries\n\n  PR #1045 was about DB credential gaps after Betterleaks. It did\n  not broadly solve transcript command shapes.\n\n  Betterleaks already catches normal OpenSSH private-key blocks\n  like:\n\n  -----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----\n  ...\n  -----END OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----\n\n  The more relevant missed case became the transcript command\n  shape where a low/moderate entropy literal is piped into a\n  secret-setting command. Entropy alone does not reliably catch\n  values like correct-horse-client or similar human-ish secrets.\n\n  GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET is a real credential and worth redacting.\n\n  CLIENT_ID, Application ID, and GOOGLE_ADSENSE_ACCOUNT=pub-...\n  are more like identifiers/accounts and should not automatically\n  be redacted unless the value itself independently looks secret-\n  like.\n\n  Current Decision Point\n\n  I think the necessary part is:\n\n  - Keep GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET key/value redaction.\n  - Keep JSONL structured-field redaction for\n    GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET.\n  - Keep the generalized printf 'REDACTED' | ... secret put API_KEY\n    transcript regression.\n  - Keep one guard proving variable references like\n    $EXAMPLE_API_KEY are preserved.\n\n  The questionable part is:\n\n  - GOOGLE_ADSENSE_ACCOUNT=pub-... preservation.\n  - high-entropy *_ACCOUNT=... still-redacts guard.\n  - isNonSecretIdentifierAssignment entropy-skip policy.\n\n  That account/id behavior is a separate over-redaction policy\n  decision, not required to fix the confirmed transcript secret\n  leak.\n\n  Verification\n\n  After the final trim:\n\n  - go test ./redact -count=1 passed.\n  - git diff --check passed.\n  - A final mise run check was started but interrupted by the user\n    after the final trim, so full check is not confirmed on the\n    latest exact tree.\n\n  Suggested Ask For Claude\n\n  Review the current diff in redact/redact.go and redact/\n  redact_test.go. Please answer whether the account/id entropy\n  guard is worth keeping, or whether we should remove it and only\n  keep the CLIENT_SECRET plus shell-stdin secret transcript\n  redaction. Focus on over-redaction risk, test clutter, and\n  whether the behavior matches existing redaction test\n  conventions."},"uuid":"fcd55361-b5ff-43cc-8a91-6b26f2ae4e7b","timestamp":"2026-05-13T20:06:19.226Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"19b7cd33-a796-49bd-9cad-3d1398001e2d","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
