{"parentUuid":"7c7308eb-4622-4fa8-bf5b-a7f9684b22ff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- test-auditor: Audits unit tests for code changed on the current branch — rates existing tests, flags useless ones for removal, and writes missing tests. Use this skill whenever the user wants to evaluate test quality, audit tests, check test effectiveness, improve test coverage for their branch, find weak or redundant tests, or asks things like \"are my tests good?\", \"do I have enough tests?\", \"audit my tests\", \"clean up my tests\", or \"what tests am I missing?\". Also trigger when the user mentions \"test coverage\", \"test gaps\", \"redundant tests\", \"flaky tests\", \"useless tests\", or \"test quality\" in the context of a feature branch.\n- test-repo: Use this skill to test strategy changes against a fresh test repository. Invoke when the user asks to \"test against a test repo\", \"validate the changes\", or wants to verify session hooks, commits, and rewind functionality work correctly.\n- changelog: Generate or update the CHANGELOG.md for a new release version. Use when the user says \"generate changelog\", \"update changelog\", \"write release notes\", or asks to prepare a changelog for a version like \"changelog for 0.5.3\".\n- e2e: Orchestrate E2E test triage and fix implementation: runs triage-ci then implement sequentially. Accepts test names, --agent, artifact path, or CI run reference. For individual phases, use /e2e:triage-ci, /e2e:debug, or /e2e:implement. Use when the user says \"triage e2e\", \"fix e2e failures\", or wants the full triage-to-fix pipeline.\n- agent-integration: Run all three agent integration phases sequentially: research, write-tests, and implement using E2E-first TDD (unit tests written last). For individual phases, use /agent-integration:research, /agent-integration:write-tests, or /agent-integration:implement. Use when the user says \"integrate agent\", \"add agent support\", or wants to run the ful